<Site title="Plan your inference evaluation"><PageIntro title="Start with your workload." text="Use this practical guide to frame an inference comparison before choosing a model, engine, or search strategy."/><section class="section content-section"><div class="guide-layout"><div><h2>A useful technical discussion<br/>starts with specific questions.</h2><ol class="guide-list"><li><strong>What are you serving?</strong> Record the model candidate and immutable revision.</li><li><strong>What does demand look like?</strong> Define input/output lengths, concurrency, prompt count, and seed.</li><li><strong>What can the hardware run?</strong> Identify observed GPU type/count and verified engine image.</li><li><strong>Which tradeoff matters?</strong> Specify throughput, E2E latency, or TTFT and any hard limits.</li><li><strong>What makes results comparable?</strong> Preserve context, serving configuration, and artifact fingerprints.</li><li><strong>How will you validate the winner?</strong> Reserve independent inference validation.</li></ol></div><aside class="panel"><h3>Take the guide with you.</h3><p>An ungated Markdown guide with a workload template, metric definitions, and the simulation formulas.</p><a class="primary-button" href="/inference-evaluation-guide.md" download>Download evaluation guide ↓</a><p class="small muted">No signup or contact information is collected. A technical-discussion link will be added when a real contact destination is available.</p></aside></div></section></Site>
